@hemanthvnp, thanks for your patience!
format_sse_event is not documented, therefore it should be considered as internal utility function.
The only one place where it's used with id and event parameters passed into it is



      fastapi/fastapi/routing.py


        Lines 518 to 538
      in
      afe4112







           if isinstance(item, ServerSentEvent): 




               # User controls the event structure. 




               # Serialize the data payload if present. 




               # For ServerSentEvent items we skip stream_item_field 




               # validation (the user may mix types intentionally). 




               if item.raw_data is not None: 




                   data_str: str | None = item.raw_data 




               elif item.data is not None: 




                   if hasattr(item.data, "model_dump_json"): 




                       data_str = item.data.model_dump_json() 




                   else: 




                       data_str = json.dumps(jsonable_encoder(item.data)) 




               else: 




                   data_str = None 




               return format_sse_event( 




                   data_str=data_str, 




                   event=item.event, 




                   id=item.id, 




                   retry=item.retry, 




                   comment=item.comment, 




               ) 





.. and the values of item.event and item.id are already validated as they come from the instance of ServerSentEvent.
So, adding this validation to format_sse_event would be redundant.
